// THE FIXED SET against every row of the article's tables: fixed/agent-policy.dw, copied below
// unchanged, with each table row replayed against the whole set. Each row supplies what the OTHER
// protections need -- a recent advisor interaction, a profile lookup, a fresh quote -- so that it
// tests exactly the protection its table is about. Verdicts are the article's; the one `finding`
// left is the response-recording delay, which no policy can fix.

// A PROPOSED CORRECTION of the article's policy set, in AgentCore's own form -- every rule scoped
// to the gateway, `eventResource: resource` in every predicate -- checked against the article's
// own decision tables (tables/00-fixed-set.dw in this directory) and against the property modules
// beside it. ../agent-policy.dw is the set as published; ../README.md says what is wrong with it.
//
// The changes, each answering one finding:
//
//   1. ONE PERMIT ON execute_trade. The article publishes four (policies 2, 3, 4, 5), and in Cedar any
//      one permit that matches grants, so each is an alternative to the others. What the article
//      describes as requirements are now: the conditions every trade needs, joined in one permit
//      (AgentCore's own idiom for "both prerequisites"); and the conditions that take access away,
//      as FORBIDs, which deny whatever any permit allows.
//   2. INTEGRITY ON WHAT WAS RETURNED. The article's text and table check the trade's portfolio_id
//      against one get_client_profile RETURNED; its policy compared input.profile_id with the
//      lookup's input. Here it is `output.portfolio_id` -- which needs get_client_profile to declare
//      an output schema with that field, or AgentCore rejects the policy.
//   3. THE BUDGET COUNTS TRADES. The article's policy summed the cost of get_market_price requests.
//      Here it sums execute_trade requests, including the one being decided, which is AgentCore's
//      own pattern for a running total -- and a forbid, so reaching the cap actually denies.
//   4. APPROVAL AS A FORBID on trades over $25,000 with no unconsumed approval. The article's
//      threshold was `cost < 25000` -- so a trade of exactly $25,000 needed approval, where the prose
//      says "exceeding $25,000"; this is `> 25000`.
//   5. TRUST DECAY THE RIGHT WAY ROUND, as a forbid: no write without an advisor interaction in the
//      last 15 minutes. The article's `permit ... unless` granted exactly when the advisor was away.
//   6. ONE SPELLING OF EACH ACTION. The article names policy 1's actions `FinTarget___...` and the
//      rest bare, so its workflow chain and its trust decay were about different rebalance actions.
//      Bare names throughout here, matching the article's other six policies and its tables. A real
//      gateway names an MCP tool `<Target>___<tool>`, so deployed, every name below takes the target
//      prefix -- consistently, which is the point.
//
// What this does NOT fix, because no policy can: AgentCore records a response "shortly after" the
// call completes, so two trades sent back to back can both find one approval unconsumed. The
// guide's advice is to wait for each response; tables/00-fixed-set.dw keeps that row as a finding.

// ---- the read-only tools, and the advisor's own actions ----------------------------------------
permit (principal, action == AgentCore::Action::"get_client_profile", resource == AgentCore::Gateway::"<GATEWAY_ARN>");
permit (principal, action == AgentCore::Action::"get_market_price", resource == AgentCore::Gateway::"<GATEWAY_ARN>");
permit (principal, action == AgentCore::Action::"interact_advisor", resource == AgentCore::Gateway::"<GATEWAY_ARN>");
permit (principal, action == AgentCore::Action::"approve_trade", resource == AgentCore::Gateway::"<GATEWAY_ARN>");

// ---- policy 1, workflow sequencing: unchanged but for the action names ---------------------------
permit (principal, action == AgentCore::Action::"load_portfolio", resource == AgentCore::Gateway::"<GATEWAY_ARN>")
when temporal {
    formerly within 5m (AgentCore::Action::"get_client_profile"::response{eventResource: resource})
};

permit (principal, action == AgentCore::Action::"rebalance_portfolio", resource == AgentCore::Gateway::"<GATEWAY_ARN>")
when temporal {
    formerly within 5m (AgentCore::Action::"load_portfolio"::response{eventResource: resource})
};

// ---- policies 2 and 3, what every trade needs: one permit -----------------------------------------
permit (
    principal,
    action == AgentCore::Action::"execute_trade",
    resource == AgentCore::Gateway::"<GATEWAY_ARN>"
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 24h AgentCore::Action::"get_client_profile"::response{
        eventResource: resource,
        output.portfolio_id: context.input.portfolio_id
    }
    && formerly within 30s AgentCore::Action::"get_market_price"::response{ eventResource: resource }
};

// ---- policy 4, the budget: a forbid, over trades ---------------------------------------------------
forbid (
    principal,
    action == AgentCore::Action::"execute_trade",
    resource == AgentCore::Gateway::"<GATEWAY_ARN>"
)
when temporal {
    exists (total: Long). (sum amount for (amount: Long), (t: Timepoint). where (formerly within 24h (
        AgentCore::Action::"execute_trade"::request{ eventResource: resource, input.cost: amount } && tp(t)))) == total
        && total > 60000
};

// ---- policy 5, approval for large trades: a forbid unless an approval is unconsumed ---------------
forbid (
    principal,
    action == AgentCore::Action::"execute_trade",
    resource == AgentCore::Gateway::"<GATEWAY_ARN>"
)
when { context.input.cost > 25000 }
unless temporal {
    !(AgentCore::Action::"execute_trade"::response{ eventResource: resource })
    since within 24h (AgentCore::Action::"approve_trade"::response{ input.status: "approved", eventResource: resource })
};

// ---- policy 7, trust decay: no write without a recent advisor interaction ------------------------
forbid (
    principal,
    action in [
        AgentCore::Action::"execute_trade",
        AgentCore::Action::"rebalance_portfolio"
    ],
    resource == AgentCore::Gateway::"<GATEWAY_ARN>"
)
unless temporal {
    formerly within 15m AgentCore::Action::"interact_advisor"::response{ eventResource: resource }
};

